-# The Knowledge Card: Groups & Problem Visibility
.card.border-0.shadow-sm.border-start.border-4.border-info
  .card-body.p-3.p-md-4

    -# --- Header ---
    .d-flex.align-items-center.flex-wrap.gap-3.mb-3
      .bg-info-subtle.text-info-emphasis.rounded-circle.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.lh-1.flex-shrink-0{style: "width: 44px; height: 44px"}
        %span.mi.md-24.fill help

      .flex-grow-1{style: "min-width: 200px;"}
        %h5.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-0 How Groups Work
        %small.text-secondary Grouping users and problems, Group Mode, and group status effects.

    -# --- Section 1: Core Concept: What Groups Do ---
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 What Groups Do
    .row.g-2.mb-3
      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-2.px-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.mi.md-20.text-primary.flex-shrink-0 hub
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark.small Linking Users & Problems
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            A group serves as a bridge, grouping and linking specific <strong>users</strong> with specific <strong>problems</strong>.

      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-2.px-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.mi.md-20.text-info.flex-shrink-0 visibility
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark.small Scoped Access & Cohorts
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            Controls problem access, targeted announcements, and dedicated scoreboards for distinct classes or cohorts.

    -# --- Section 2: Problem Group Mode (Enabled vs Disabled) ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    .d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-between.flex-wrap.gap-2.mb-2
      %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-0 Problem Group Mode Configuration
      .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.flex-wrap
        %small.text-secondary Current Status:
        - if GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group?
          %span.badge.bg-success-subtle.text-success.border.border-success-subtle On (Enabled)
        - else
          %span.badge.bg-secondary-subtle.text-secondary.border.border-secondary-subtle Off (Disabled)
        = link_to grader_configuration_index_path, class: 'btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm py-0 px-2' do
          %span.mi.md-14 settings
          Config

    .row.g-2.mb-3
      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-2.px-3.rounded-3.border.h-100{class: GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group? ? 'bg-light' : 'border-primary-subtle bg-primary-subtle bg-opacity-10', style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.badge.bg-secondary Off (Default)
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark.small Open Ungrouped Problems
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            Ungrouped problems are public to all students. Grouped problems stay member-only.

      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-2.px-3.rounded-3.border.h-100{class: GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group? ? 'border-success-subtle bg-success-subtle bg-opacity-10' : 'bg-light', style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.badge.bg-success On
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark.small Strict Isolation
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            Ungrouped problems are hidden from students; students only see problems in their assigned groups.

    -# --- Section 3: Group Status (Enabled vs Disabled) ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 Group Status: Effects of Enabling & Disabling a Group
    .row.g-3.mb-3
      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.h-100.border-success-subtle.bg-success-subtle.bg-opacity-10{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-2
            %span.mi.md-20.text-success.flex-shrink-0 check_circle
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark When a Group is Enabled (Active)
          %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
            %li <strong>Problem Access:</strong> Members can view and submit to enabled problems in the group.
            %li <strong>Announcements:</strong> Group-targeted announcements are visible on members' dashboard.
            %li <strong>Scoreboard & Reports:</strong> Scores and rankings appear on group scoreboards and reports.

      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.h-100.border-danger-subtle.bg-danger-subtle.bg-opacity-10{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-2
            %span.mi.md-20.text-danger.flex-shrink-0 cancel
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark When a Group is Disabled (Inactive)
          %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
            %li <strong>Problem Access Revoked:</strong> Members lose access to problems scoped solely by this group.
            %li <strong>Announcements Hidden:</strong> Group-targeted announcements are hidden from students.
            %li <strong>Scoreboard Excluded:</strong> Members are removed from group scoreboard rankings and totals.

    -# --- Section 4: Fine-Grained Controls ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 Fine-Grained Controls Inside a Group
    .row.g-3
      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
            %span.mi.md-18.text-warning.flex-shrink-0 toggle_on
            %small.text-secondary
              %strong.text-dark Problem-level Enabled Toggle:
              Within a group's problem list, you can individually enable or disable specific problems without disabling the whole group.
      .col-12.col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100{style: "min-width: 0; word-break: break-word;"}
          .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
            %span.mi.md-18.text-info.flex-shrink-0 person_off
            %small.text-secondary
              %strong.text-dark Member-level Enabled Toggle:
              Individual user memberships in a group can be toggled on or off to suspend a specific user's group privileges without removing them.
